      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Pain is one of the most common complaints that cause patients to seek care in the emergency department. Research and patient complaints however, continue to demonstrate that pain management needs improvement. This article addresses pain management in emergency care. It presents both pharmacologic and nonpharmacologic methods of pain management."},
